item.description:
&ldquo;Spring Boot is magic&rdquo; is something you hear a lot. Add spring-boot-starter-data-jpa and suddenly you have a working DataSource, a JpaTransactionManager, and a LocalContainerEntityManagerFactoryBean — without writing a single @Bean method. Understanding how this actually works turns the magic into a tool you can control, debug, and extend.
The Entry Point: @EnableAutoConfiguration @SpringBootApplication is a shorthand for three annotations:
@Configuration @EnableAutoConfiguration // this is the one that matters here @ComponentScan public class MyApplication { public static void main(String[] args) { SpringApplication.
